1
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,720
How Life Began on the Earth

2
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:13,140
No one knows exactly how the Earth began, as it happened so long ago.

3
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,580
However, according to a widely accepted theory,

4
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:21,820
the universe began with a "Big Bang" that threw matter in all directions.

5
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:27,000
After that, atoms began to form and combine to create stars

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,920
and other bodies.

7
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:32,060
For several billion years after the "Big Bang",

8
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,580
the earth was still just a cloud of dust.

9
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:42,520
What it was to become was uncertain until between 4.5 and 3.8 billion years ago

10
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,140
when the dust settled into a solid globe.

11
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:51,360
The earth became so violent that it was not clear whether the shape would last or not.

12
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,600
It exploded loudly with fire and rock.

13
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:58,340
They were in time to produce carbon,

14
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,700
nitrogen, water vapour and other gases,

15
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,100
which were to make the earth’s atmosphere.

16
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:09,460
What is even more important is that as the earth cooled down,

17
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:12,120
water began to appear on its surface.

18
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:17,500
Water had also appeared on other planets like Mars but,

19
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,200
unlike the earth, it had disappeared later.

20
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:26,400
It was not immediately obvious that water was to be fundamental to the development of life.

21
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:33,900
What many scientists believe is that the continued presence of water allowed the Earth to dissolve

22
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,680
and acids into the oceans and seas.

23
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,700
This produced a chain reaction,

24
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:43,460
which made it possible for life to develop.

25
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:47,020
Many millions of years later,

26
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:51,800
the first extremely small plants began to appear on the surface of the water.

27
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:56,560
They multiplied and filled the oceans and seas with oxygen,

28
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:01,660
which encouraged the later development of early shellfish and all sorts of fish.

29
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:05,160
Next, green plants began to grow on land.

30
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,440
They were followed in time by land animals.

31
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,660
Some were insects.

32
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:16,940
Others, called amphibians, were able to live on land as well as in the water.

33
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,940
Later when the plants grew into forests,

34
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,280
reptiles appeared for the first time.

35
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:29,920
After that, some huge animals, called dinosaurs,

36
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,460
developed.

37
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:37,440
They laid eggs too and existed on the earth for more than 140 million years.

38
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:43,220
However, 65 million years ago the age of the dinosaurs ended.

39
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:47,880
Why they suddenly disappeared still remains a mystery.

40
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:52,820
This disappearance made possible the rise of mammals on the earth.

41
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:57,100
These animals were different from all life forms in the past,

42
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:02,500
because they gave birth to young baby animals and produced milk to feed them.

43
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:09,320
Finally about 2.6 million years ago some small clever animals,

44
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,460
now with hands and feet, appeared and spread all over the earth.

45
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:18,780
Thus they have, in their turn, become the most important animals on the planet.

46
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:23,060
But they are not looking after the earth very well.

47
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,920
They are putting too much carbon dioxide into the atmosphere,

48
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,820
which prevents heat from escaping from the earth into space.

49
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:37,520
As a result of this, many scientists believe the earth may become too hot to live on.

50
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:43,340
So, whether life will continue on the Earth for millions of years to come will depend

51
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,600
on whether this problem can be solved.
